From: ProjectM TV contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Use MilkDrop gamma-only pass-count epsilon

Follow MilkDrop 2.25c milkdropfs.cpp:4245: gamma-only pass count uses
.001f, distinct from echo redraws' .0001f. Preserve echo behavior,
live gamma values, tint repair0014, float diffuse policy and blends.
At loaded gamma1.0005 this removes a redundant fullscreen pass; at
2.001 it restores two passes with the original final weight instead
of three. Do not quantize diffuse attributes as part of this change.

Original source: milkdrop2 f05b0d8, milkdropfs.cpp SHA256
68749d31bb6b3020ca89b1e7630fd704e58a5de8dd6275c9f5ea005c6586a7d9.

---
diff --git a/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/VideoEcho.cpp b/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/VideoEcho.cpp
index 139af7b7a..99d5f00a1 100644
--- a/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/VideoEcho.cpp
+++ b/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/VideoEcho.cpp
@@ -210,7 +210,8 @@ void VideoEcho::DrawGammaAdjustment(const PerFrameContext& perFrameContext)
     Renderer::BlendMode::Set(true, Renderer::BlendMode::Function::One, Renderer::BlendMode::Function::Zero);
 
     auto const gammaAdj = static_cast<float>(*perFrameContext.gamma);
-    int const redrawCount = static_cast<int>(gammaAdj - 0.0001f) + 1;
+    // MilkDrop's gamma-only path has a distinct epsilon from echo redraws.
+    int const redrawCount = static_cast<int>(gammaAdj - 0.001f) + 1;
 
     for (int redraw = 0; redraw < redrawCount; redraw++)
     {

